SUMMARY:In the Room: Sixty Years on the Front Lines of History
DESCRIPTION:In person · Paid · Included with general admission\n\nRooseve
 lt understood the camera before most politicians did. He posed in buckskin
  in the Badlands\, stood with John Muir at Yosemite\, and left behind one 
 of the most photographed lives of his century. David Hume Kennerly…\n\nL
 isted by Theodore Roosevelt Presidential Library\n\nhttps://www.trlibrary.
 com/calendar/daily-activity/room-sixty-years-front-lines-history
LOCATION:Theodore Roosevelt Presidential Library\, 3410 Chateau Rd\, Medora
 \, ND
